# import vm from "node:vm"; vm.read(f, "constructor")("return 1");        node:vm: export default { read: (subject, key) => subject[key] };
# The library reads under a key that it is handed, off a value that it is handed, and what it finds goes back to the program. The key is a text that the program has written, so it is a name that the program spells:
# `EventEmitter.prototype.listeners.call({ _events: function () {} }, "constructor")[0]("return 6 * 7")()`. If only the names of accesses counted, the image would admit no text, and the run time would refuse what plain Bun runs
